01:39:37,210 --> 01:39:42,210
Deterministic effect of radiation exposure is defined as the effect that increase in severity.
辐射照射的确定性效应定义为，严重程度

879
01:39:42,210 --> 01:39:45,210
With increasing absorb those in the effect tissue.
随受影响组织吸收剂量的增加而加重的效应。

880
01:39:45,210 --> 01:39:48,210
And usually has a minimum threshold value.
通常有一个最低阈值。

881
01:39:48,210 --> 01:39:51,210
Below this threshold the effect is not seen.
低于这个阈值就看不到这种效应。

882
01:39:51,210 --> 01:39:57,210
Deterministic effect attributable to exposure to ionizing radiation.
可归因于电离辐射照射的确定性效应

883
01:39:57,210 --> 01:40:05,210
It includes skin, reddening, tissue, incrosis, hair loss, cataract, blood abnormalities.
包括皮肤发红、组织坏死、脱发、白内障、血液异常，

884
01:40:05,210 --> 01:40:08,210
And the decrease in sperm production in the male.
以及男性精子生成减少。

885
01:40:08,210 --> 01:40:11,210
Like for cataract, what is the threshold for cataract?
比如白内障，白内障的阈值是多少？

886
01:40:11,210 --> 01:40:24,660
Anyone knows?
有人知道吗？

887
01:40:24,660 --> 01:40:36,630
I cataract.
眼部白内障。

888
01:40:36,630 --> 01:40:42,630
Tin and gray, Doris, this is correct in the protocols.
10 戈瑞，Doris，这在规程里是对的。

889
01:40:42,630 --> 01:40:47,630
They are writing that tin and gray will cause cataract.
规程里写的是 10 戈瑞会导致白内障。

890
01:40:47,630 --> 01:40:58,210
Or the lenses are gone.
或者说晶状体就坏了。

891
01:40:58,210 --> 01:40:59,210
Okay.
好。

892
01:40:59,210 --> 01:41:02,210
Let's start from 2.5 gray and above.
我们从 2.5 戈瑞及以上开始。

893
01:41:02,210 --> 01:41:04,210
From 2.5 gray and above.
从 2.5 戈瑞及以上。

894
01:41:04,210 --> 01:41:09,210
If the lens is directly related to this, this may cause cataract.
如果晶状体直接受到照射，就可能导致白内障。

895
01:41:09,210 --> 01:41:15,210
And you could see this easily with the people who are working with the fluoroscopy.
在从事透视工作的人身上很容易看到这一点。

896
01:41:15,210 --> 01:41:20,210
Most of them have a problem with their lenses and so on.
他们大多数人的晶状体都有问题等等。

897
01:41:20,210 --> 01:41:28,300
The threshold of deterministic effect.
确定性效应的阈值。

898
01:41:28,300 --> 01:41:30,300
Cataract of the lens of the eye.
眼晶状体白内障，

899
01:41:30,300 --> 01:41:32,300
From 2 to 10.
从 2 到 10。

900
01:41:32,300 --> 01:41:35,300
This is what we said, Doris.
这就是我们刚才说的，Doris。

901
01:41:35,300 --> 01:41:36,300
Tin and gray in the protocol.
规程里是 10 戈瑞。

902
01:41:36,300 --> 01:41:40,300
But usually from 2 gray, this happens.
但通常从 2 戈瑞起就会发生。

903
01:41:40,300 --> 01:41:42,300
Yes, and geography the same.
是的，血管造影也一样。

904
01:41:42,300 --> 01:41:45,470
Thank you.
谢谢。

905
01:41:45,470 --> 01:41:47,470
Permanent sterility.
永久性不育。

906
01:41:47,470 --> 01:41:52,470
For males from 3.5 to 6 Sievert, we have permanent sterility.
男性在 3.5 到 6 希沃特会出现永久性不育。

907
01:41:52,470 --> 01:41:55,470
For females from 2.5 to 6.
女性是 2.5 到 6。

908
01:41:55,470 --> 01:41:57,470
Temporary sterility.
暂时性不育。

909
01:41:57,470 --> 01:42:01,470
For males, we have around 1.15 Sievert.
男性大约是 1.15 希沃特。

910
01:42:01,470 --> 01:42:03,470
For females, we have 1.6 Sievert.
女性是 1.6 希沃特。

911
01:42:03,470 --> 01:42:14,280
So the females are more radiation resistant to sterility than men.
所以在不育方面，女性比男性更耐受辐射。

912
01:42:14,280 --> 01:42:17,280
Note that the threshold may differ from one person to another.
注意，阈值可能因人而异。

913
01:42:17,280 --> 01:42:21,280
That's why it's coming as tolerance from 2.
这就是为什么它是从 2 开始的一个容许范围。

914
01:42:21,280 --> 01:42:23,280
It's not fixed number.
不是一个固定的数字。

915
01:42:26,320 --> 01:42:28,320
Stochastic effect.
随机性效应。

916
01:42:28,320 --> 01:42:33,320
These effects, which are generally delayed or latent in nature,
这些效应通常本质上是迟发的或潜伏的，

917
01:42:33,320 --> 01:42:37,320
are defined as the effect in which the probability of occurrence,
其定义是：效应发生的概率

918
01:42:37,320 --> 01:42:41,320
and the severity of the effect, is a function of radiation dose without threshold.
以及效应的严重程度是辐射剂量的函数，没有阈值。

919
01:42:41,320 --> 01:42:43,320
So here we don't have a threshold.
所以这里没有阈值。

920
01:42:43,320 --> 01:42:46,320
In the deterministic or non-stochastic, we have a threshold.
在确定性效应或非随机性效应中，是有阈值的。

921
01:42:46,320 --> 01:42:47,320
Before that, nothing happened.
在阈值之前，什么都不会发生。

922
01:42:47,320 --> 01:42:49,320
In the stochastic, no threshold.
在随机性效应中，没有阈值。

923
01:42:49,320 --> 01:42:54,370
It can happen in low dose, it can happen in high dose, and so on.
低剂量时可能发生，高剂量时也可能发生，等等。

924
01:42:54,370 --> 01:42:59,370
Examples, cancers, solid malignant tumors, and leukemia.
例如癌症、实体恶性肿瘤和白血病。

925
01:42:59,370 --> 01:43:05,370
Heritable genetic effects are graded as the main stochastic effect
可遗传的遗传效应被列为电离辐射照射

926
01:43:05,370 --> 01:43:09,370
from exposure to ionizing radiation.
主要的随机性效应。

927
01:43:09,370 --> 01:43:19,370
Heritable effects were considered most important in 1950s and 1960s.
在 20 世纪 50 年代和 60 年代，遗传效应被认为是最重要的。

928
01:43:19,370 --> 01:43:22,970
Bismatic effect.
躯体效应。

929
01:43:22,970 --> 01:43:26,970
This is a normal cell being exposed to radiation.
这是一个受到辐射照射的正常细胞。

930
01:43:26,970 --> 01:43:31,970
The cell became mutated or the cell died.
细胞发生了突变，或者细胞死亡了。

931
01:43:31,970 --> 01:43:35,970
Biological effects that appear in the exposed version.
出现在受照者本人身上的生物效应。

932
01:43:35,970 --> 01:43:41,970
Examples, cells become cancerous, or cell death, or cataract formation.
例如细胞癌变、细胞死亡或形成白内障，

933
01:43:41,970 --> 01:43:44,970
Increased susceptibility to disease.
对疾病的易感性增加。

934
01:43:44,970 --> 01:43:49,970
And somatic effect may result from either acute or chronic dose radiation.
躯体效应可能由急性或慢性剂量辐射引起。

935
01:43:49,970 --> 01:43:57,370
The heritable effects from it, heritable, so it goes to the next generation,
遗传效应，可遗传的，也就是会传给下一代，

936
01:43:57,370 --> 01:44:04,100
biological effects that are inherited by children from their parents at conception.
是孩子在受孕时从父母那里遗传的生物效应。

937
01:44:04,100 --> 01:44:11,100
A radiation of reproductive organs can damage, alter the cells involved in conception,
生殖器官受到辐射会损伤、改变与受孕有关的细胞，

938
01:44:11,100 --> 01:44:14,100
and can alter genetic information.
并可能改变遗传信息。

939
01:44:14,100 --> 01:44:23,100
Heritable health effect that have been observed in humans based upon animal data
在人类身上观察到的遗传健康效应是基于动物数据的，

940
01:44:23,100 --> 01:44:29,100
and assumption is made that heritable effect could occur in humans.
并假定遗传效应可能会发生在人类身上。

941
01:44:29,100 --> 01:44:38,100
So all the experiments being done in animals, and they make the assumption that this may have been in humans.
所以所有的实验都是在动物身上做的，他们假定这在人类身上也可能发生。

942
01:44:38,100 --> 01:44:46,450
Factors that determine the biological effect of radiation.
决定辐射生物效应的因素：

943
01:44:46,450 --> 01:44:48,450
Area of the body exposed.
受照的身体部位，

944
01:44:48,450 --> 01:44:50,450
Sensitivity.
敏感性，

945
01:44:50,450 --> 01:44:52,450
Individual sensitivity.
个体敏感性，

946
01:44:52,450 --> 01:44:54,450
Types and energy of radiation.
辐射的类型和能量，

947
01:44:54,450 --> 01:44:57,450
As we said, alpha is 20 times than that of photons.
正如我们说过的，阿尔法是光子的 20 倍，

948
01:44:57,450 --> 01:45:00,450
Total dose received.
受到的总剂量，

949
01:45:00,450 --> 01:45:01,450
Dose rate.
剂量率。

950
01:45:01,450 --> 01:45:10,140
The high dose rate, it means this is acute rather than chronic for a longer time.
高剂量率意味着这是急性照射，而不是长时间的慢性照射。

951
01:45:10,140 --> 01:45:13,140
Relative sensitivity of the cell and tissue type.
细胞和组织类型的相对敏感性。

952
01:45:13,140 --> 01:45:17,140
So we have lymphocytes, bermatogonia, hematobiotic, the blood forming.
有淋巴细胞、精原细胞、造血细胞，也就是造血组织。

953
01:45:17,140 --> 01:45:20,140
So let's see this sample.
我们来看这个示意图。

954
01:45:20,140 --> 01:45:24,140
So these are more sensitive, and this is the least sensitive.
这些更敏感，这个最不敏感。

955
01:45:24,140 --> 01:45:26,140
So the collagen is the least sensitive.
胶原最不敏感。

956
01:45:26,140 --> 01:45:28,140
Bone is the least sensitive.
骨最不敏感。

957
01:45:28,140 --> 01:45:31,140
Whether the lymphocytes is more sensitive to radiation.
而淋巴细胞对辐射更敏感。

958
01:45:31,140 --> 01:45:34,140
That's why for lymphoma, how much dose we are giving?
所以对于淋巴瘤，我们给多少剂量？

959
01:45:34,140 --> 01:45:42,180
Almost around 20 gray.
大约 20 戈瑞左右。

960
01:45:42,180 --> 01:45:44,180
We are giving for the lymphoma, usually.
我们通常给淋巴瘤的剂量就是这样。

961
01:45:44,180 --> 01:45:50,180
Whereas for the bone, like sarcoma and so on, we reach sometimes up to 70 gray.
而对于骨，比如肉瘤之类的，我们有时会达到 70 戈瑞。

962
01:45:50,180 --> 01:45:58,970
Because they are radio resistant.
因为它们是抗辐射的。

